# Licensing and Trial Registry

## Purpose

Closed-network installs: Ed25519 JWT on disk; no license server ping. Module and product id: **ad-event-processor**. Customer file: `var/license.jwt` (not repo root).

Hot path reads inline license snapshot only - not `IngestAllowed()` per request. Tracker garble off; control/processor garble on (`release_strings_gate`).

## License states

| State | Tracking |
| :--- | :--- |
| ACTIVE | Normal operation |
| GRACE | JWT expired within `grace_days` (7) |
| EXPIRED | Blocked |

Pilot SKU (`deploy/vendor/sku.yaml`): 10 days, 5k RPS, OpenRTB off, hard bind optional.

## Issue JWT (vendor)

```bash
export AD_EVENT_PROCESSOR_LICENSE_PRIVATE_KEY_FILE=deploy/vendor/license_private.key
go run ./cmd/license-issue \
 --sku pilot --customer "Acme" \
 --deployment-id "<uuid>" --hwid-v2 "<hwid>" \
 --out /tmp/acme.jwt
```

Reuse same `deployment_id` on renewals and tier upgrades. HWID v2 (Argon2id) preferred over legacy fingerprint when JWT has `hwid_hash`.

## Verification catalog

Gate: `make license-verify`, `make license-red-team`.

| ID | Property |
| :--- | :--- |
| P-C2-01 | Invalid signature or payload => reject |
| P-C3-03 | `IngestAllowed` false iff state in {EXPIRED, REVOKED} |
| P-C4-03 | Customer limits never exceed deployment ceiling |
| P-HWID-01 | Argon2id hash deterministic for fixed telemetry |

Status API: `GET /api/v1/license/status` (fields include `host_fingerprint`, `hwid_v2`, `hwid_match`, `days_to_expiry`).

## Release guard kill switches

Lab gdb/strace/delve on garbled builds:

| Env | Effect |
| :--- | :--- |
| `AD_EVENT_PROCESSOR_LICENSE_GUARD=0` | Disable all probes |
| `AD_EVENT_PROCESSOR_LICENSE_GUARD_PTRACE=0` | Disable ptrace watchdog only |

## Trial registry (vendor plane)

Repeat-trial defense at **JWT issue time**, not on buyer VPS.

| Anchor | Use |
| :--- | :--- |
| `telegram` | Primary identity |
| `deployment_id` | Links pilot -> paid |
| `hwid` | Block second pilot on same metal |
| `usdt_tx` | One wallet -> one buyer line |

Env: `VENDOR_TRIAL_REGISTRY=deploy/vendor/trial_registry.json`. Force re-issue: `VENDOR_TRIAL_FORCE=1` + `--force --force-reason`.

Reject pilot when prior `telegram` or `hwid` with status `active|expired`; same wallet on prior pilot. Do not hard-block IP /24 alone.

CLI: `trial-registry list-pending`, `license-issue --approve-pending`, `--record-hwid`, `--mark-converted`.

## Tier ladder (USDT / month)

| SKU | USDT/mo | Hosts | Peak RPS |
| :--- | ---: | ---: | ---: |
| starter | $129 | 1 | 10k |
| pro | $329 | 1 | 25k |
| scale | $649 | 3 | 75k |
| network | $1,199 | 10 | 150k |
| enterprise | $2,500+ | 99 | custom |
| pilot | $0 | 1 | 5k (10 days) |

Enforcement: hosts + peak RPS + feature gates (OpenRTB, ML, eBPF). Unlimited campaigns on self-hosted - quote RPS and hosts only.

Cryptomus webhook: vendor VPS only; verify `sign`; idempotency on `uuid`; JWT only on `paid` / `paid_over`. Appliance `POST /api/v1/selfserve/payment-intents` is ledger top-up, not license renewal.

## Customer apply

Admin Settings -> License, or `license-apply`, or `POST /api/v1/license/apply`. No restart - entitlements reload immediately.

Install env: `AD_EVENT_PROCESSOR_LICENSE_MODE=file`, `TELEMETRY_ENABLED=false` default.

